Apply glPointSize to the batch it was called on, not to whatever is pending.

gl4es defers immediate-mode geometry into a renderlist and draws it later, and
the point size reaches the GLES2 fixed-pipeline shader as the gl_Point.size
uniform, uploaded from glstate at draw time (fpe.c's builtin_pointsprite.size).
gl4es_glPointSize therefore only wrote glstate and returned: a size set after a
glBegin/glEnd batch but before its flush was applied to the points already in
that batch. The last size before the flush won, for every point in it.

That is a conformance break with desktop GL, where point size is fixed per
primitive when the primitive is issued, and it is easy to hit: a pass that
draws points and then politely restores glPointSize(1.0f) shrinks its own
points to one pixel. gl-repl's vertex-marker overlays did exactly that, and
looked like "gl4es cannot draw points" until the trailing reset was isolated as
the trigger -- points render fine with no reset, and collapse with one.

glPointParameterfv in the same file already handles this correctly, so follow
it exactly rather than inventing a mechanism:

  - when compiling a display list, record the size as a renderlist op
    (pointsize_op / pointsize_val, set by rlPointSizeOp, replayed in
    listdraw.c beside the pointparam op) and return;
  - otherwise flush the pending immediate-mode batch before the state changes.

The op shares STAGE_POINTPARAM, which is an exclusive stage, so a second size
in one list starts a new renderlist rather than overwriting the first; the
merge-compatibility test in list.c refuses to merge a list carrying the op, for
the same reason it refuses one carrying a pointparam op.

Verified in headless Chrome (ANGLE/SwiftShader, WebGL2): a scene drawing four
16px GL_POINTS and then calling glPointSize(1) renders one-pixel dots before
the patch and four full-size round points after it, with GL_POINT_SMOOTH
enabled or not.

Applied by scripts/web-deps.sh after cloning the pinned gl4es checkout.
--- a/src/gl/pointsprite.c
+++ b/src/gl/pointsprite.c
@@ -121,6 +121,18 @@
         errorShim(GL_INVALID_VALUE);
         return;
     }
+    // The point size reaches the shader as the gl_Point.size uniform, uploaded
+    // from glstate at draw time -- so a size set while a renderlist is pending
+    // would apply to points already recorded in it. Handle the list exactly as
+    // glPointParameterfv above does: record it when compiling, flush the
+    // pending immediate-mode batch otherwise.
+    if (glstate->list.active) {
+        if (glstate->list.compiling) {
+            NewStage(glstate->list.active, STAGE_POINTPARAM);
+            rlPointSizeOp(glstate->list.active, size);
+            return;
+        } else gl4es_flush();
+    }
     glstate->pointsprite.size = size;
     errorGL();
     LOAD_GLES_FPE(glPointSize);
